    "reader_note": "A SET, not a single id, and it legitimately contains a Haiku model alongside the requested Sonnet. The CLI runs a second model for its own internal work, and ClaudeCLIClient._resolved_model reports whichever model emitted the most output tokens in that call -- for a one-line reader answer that is sometimes the internal model rather than the one that answered. So this field bounds which models were involved; it does not prove which produced a given answer. The requested alias is recorded verbatim under role_models. Recorded as a known imprecision rather than resolved by guessing."
